# QuicBaaS Agent Daemon Environment File
#
# Install to /etc/quicbaas/agent.env; the packaged systemd unit reads it
# via EnvironmentFile= and expands each variable into the `quicbaas agent
# serve` command line. The same variables configure the container image
# (deployments/agent-daemon/Dockerfile) when passed with `docker run -e`.
#
#   sudo mkdir -p /etc/quicbaas
#   sudo install -m 0640 -o root -g quicbaas-agent \
#     agent.env.sample /etc/quicbaas/agent.env
#   sudoedit /etc/quicbaas/agent.env
#
# Format is KEY=value, one per line, no shell quoting: systemd passes the
# value through verbatim, so `QUICBAAS_TENANT="acme"` sets the tenant to
# the five characters "acme" including the quotes.
#
# There is no YAML configuration file. `quicbaas agent serve` is
# configured by flags, and this file is how the packaged deployments
# supply them; every flag named below is checked against the live command
# by the drift gate in cmd/quicbaas/agent_serve_deployment_test.go.

# =============================================================================
# REQUIRED
# =============================================================================

# --server: HTTPS endpoint of the QuicBaaS server this agent registers with
# and heartbeats into. Must be reachable from this host.
QUICBAAS_SERVER=https://quicbaas.example.com:8443

# --tenant: the tenant this daemon serves. Spawn requests for any other
# tenant are rejected.
QUICBAAS_TENANT=acme

# =============================================================================
# mTLS IDENTITY
# =============================================================================
#
# The daemon authenticates with a client certificate issued by the
# server's CA. There is no bootstrap token and no device certificate: the
# one-shot enrollment path was removed when agent identity became mTLS.
#
# Install the three files into the credentials directory before first
# start. They are the same basenames `quicbaas agent deploy` uploads, so a
# host provisioned by hand and one provisioned over SSH look identical:
#
#   /var/lib/quicbaas-agent/agent.crt       client certificate
#   /var/lib/quicbaas-agent/agent.key       private key, mode 0600
#   /var/lib/quicbaas-agent/server-ca.crt   CA bundle trusted for --server
#
# Override the paths only if the material lives elsewhere.

# --agent-cert
#QUICBAAS_AGENT_CERT=/var/lib/quicbaas-agent/agent.crt

# --agent-key
#QUICBAAS_AGENT_KEY=/var/lib/quicbaas-agent/agent.key

# --server-ca
#QUICBAAS_SERVER_CA=/var/lib/quicbaas-agent/server-ca.crt

# =============================================================================
# OPTIONAL — defaulted
# =============================================================================
# Each of these has the default shown; uncomment to override.

# --bind: local address for the AgentRuntime gRPC service. 127.0.0.1
# keeps it host-local; the packaged unit and image default to all
# interfaces because the control plane dials in.
#QUICBAAS_BIND_ADDR=0.0.0.0:9091

# --backends: comma-separated backends to enable. "acp" covers the
# claude / codex / opencode CLIs; "ollama" the local inference API.
#QUICBAAS_BACKENDS=acp,ollama

# --sandbox-policy: required | preferred | opt-in.
#   required  DEFAULT resolves to container-sandboxed; NONE forbidden
#   preferred DEFAULT resolves to container-sandboxed; NONE allowed
#   opt-in    DEFAULT resolves to raw exec; NONE allowed (least secure)
#QUICBAAS_SANDBOX_POLICY=required

# --container-runtime: docker | podman | auto | none. "auto" probes for
# docker, then podman. Requires the runtime socket to be reachable.
#QUICBAAS_CONTAINER_RUNTIME=auto

# --work-dir (container image only; the systemd unit pins its own under
# the state directory). Session workspaces, scratch, and the persisted
# registration credentials live here.
#QUICBAAS_WORK_DIR=/var/lib/quicbaas-agent

# --agent-cert / --agent-key / --server-ca directory (container image
# only). The unit takes the three paths individually above.
#QUICBAAS_CREDENTIALS_DIR=/etc/quicbaas/agent

# =============================================================================
# OPTIONAL — flag omitted entirely when unset
# =============================================================================

# --sandbox-network: bridge (default) | none | host | <network name>.
# "host" shares this machine's network namespace with the container,
# exposing every loopback-bound service on it to the agent. Set it only
# where those services are already inside the agent's trust boundary.
#QUICBAAS_SANDBOX_NETWORK=bridge

# --allowed-mount-root: absolute host directories a sandboxed spawn may
# bind-mount from, comma-separated. Every requested work_dir and extra
# mount must resolve under one of these, with symlinks followed first.
# Unset denies every host mount — the container runs as the daemon's own
# uid, so an unchecked mount root is this host's filesystem, read-write,
# for the agent. Not tenant-scoped: every tenant this daemon serves may
# mount from every root listed.
#QUICBAAS_ALLOWED_MOUNT_ROOTS=/srv/agent-workspaces

# --auto-pull: set to any non-empty value to pull missing container
# images at startup instead of failing the first spawn that needs one.
#QUICBAAS_AUTO_PULL=1

# --image-map: comma-separated backend=image pairs resolving which image
# a sandboxed spawn runs when the request names none.
#QUICBAAS_IMAGE_MAP=claude-code=quicbaas/claude-code:v1,codex=quicbaas/codex:v1

# --image-registry: prefix applied to unqualified image references, so
# an image map of "claude-code=claude-code:v1" resolves under it.
#QUICBAAS_IMAGE_REGISTRY=ghcr.io/automatethethings

# --mcp-endpoint: fully-qualified https://host:port/mcp address spawned
# agents dial for the "quicbaas" MCP preset. Unset leaves the preset
# unresolved, which is the default for non-MCP deployments.
#QUICBAAS_MCP_ENDPOINT=https://quicbaas.example.com:8443/mcp

# --heartbeat-interval: how often the daemon refreshes its fleet-registry
# last-seen timestamp. Default 30s.
#QUICBAAS_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL=30s
